    "sentence_translations": [
      "Avoid Saying “Thank You”?",
      "",
      "When someone helps you, you say “thank you”. This is a very natural thing.",
      "But in China, the better you know someone, the more seldom you say “thank you”.",
      "Sometimes people do not like that you say thank you.",
      "For example, some boyfriends especially do not like when their girlfriends say thank you to them.",
      "They believe that couples do not need to be so explicit and treat each other like strangers.",
      "When you say “thank you” you get a sense of distance, and that you are not intimate.",
      "",
      "Of course a lot of people also think that saying “thank you” is polite, and that you should say it if someone helps you.",
      "A lot of people will also feel uneasy if they do not say “thank you”.",
      "So what can you do if your boyfriend doesn't like that you say “thank you”? What can you say instead?",
      "How about rephrasing and using for example “you are so kind” to express your feelings of gratitude.",
      ""
    ]
  }
